/*
🔹 Time Complexity

O(n)
Each station is processed once, no restarts.

🔹 Space Complexity

O(1)
Only constant extra variables.

🔹 Intuition (step-by-step)

Treat each station as gain = gas[i] − cost[i]

totalGas checks if a solution is even possible

curGas tracks gas from the current candidate start

If curGas < 0 at index i:

You cannot reach i+1 from start

All starts in [start … i] are invalid

Move start = i + 1 and reset curGas

After one pass:

If total gas ≥ total cost → start works

Else → no solution
*/
class Solution {
    public int canCompleteCircuit(int[] gas, int[] cost) {
        int curGas = 0;
        int totalGas = 0;
        int start = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < gas.length; i++) {
            int diff = gas[i] - cost[i];
            curGas += diff;
            totalGas += diff;

            // fail at i → skip all starts from start..i
            if (curGas < 0) {
                start = i + 1;
                curGas = 0;
            }
        }

        return totalGas >= 0 ? start : -1;
    }
}
